{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedCascadeRightInverse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedCascadeRightInverse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRowRightInverse","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReverseCascade"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_uninsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_uninsert","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeRightInverse.lean#L160-L236","doc":"**The cascade right inverse.** If the reverse cascade at row `i` displaces `z`, re-inserting\n`z` rebuilds `T`.\n\nTogether with brick 2's `uninsert_insert` this makes `insert` and `uninsert` mutually inverse on a\ncolumn-strict tableau: brick 2 gives `uninsert ∘ insert = id`, which supports injectivity, and this\ngives `insert ∘ uninsert = id`, which is what surjectivity needs.\n\nThe induction mirrors brick 2's. Above the target row each step is undone by brick 9's\n`rowInsert_rowUninsert`. At the target row there are two cases: a row that keeps a cell is rebuilt\nby `insert_dropLast` with no bump, and a row that is deleted is rebuilt by\n`insert_eq_cons_of_colStrict`, which is where column strictness is spent.\n\nThe `obtain ⟨_, _, h⟩ : ∃ …, … = (…, …) := ⟨_, _, rfl⟩` idiom names the intermediate results\n*without* touching the goal; `rcases h : e with ⟨…⟩` would substitute `e` in the goal but not in\nthe hypotheses, which leaves the two out of step under the nested `match`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_eq_cons_of_colStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_eq_cons_of_colStrict","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeRightInverse.lean#L130-L158","doc":"**Re-inserting a deleted top cell rebuilds a single column.** `insert` only ever appends rows\nat the *bottom*, so `insert T a = [a] :: T` needs every row of `T` to be a single cell strictly\nabove the next — which is what `ColStrict` gives once the top row has length one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.strictBelow_head_of_colStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.strictBelow_head_of_colStrict","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeRightInverse.lean#L117-L128","doc":"The head-to-head column comparison carried by `ColStrict`, in the form the single-column\nrecursion consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_succ_of_none","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_succ_of_none","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeRightInverse.lean#L112-L115","doc":"And if the recursion itself reports nothing, so does the cascade. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_succ_of_none_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_succ_of_none_row","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeRightInverse.lean#L103-L110","doc":"The non-bumping branch: if reverse insertion into `r` finds nothing to displace, the cascade\nreports `none`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_succ_of_some","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsert_succ_of_some","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeRightInverse.lean#L91-L101","doc":"**The bumping branch of the reverse cascade, spelled out.** When the recursion below row `r`\ndisplaces `y` and reverse-inserting `y` into `r` displaces `v`, the whole cascade at row `i + 1`\nis `(r' :: T', some v)`.\n\nStating this separately keeps the main induction from having to rewrite under a `match`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_dropLast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_dropLast","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeRightInverse.lean#L83-L89","doc":"**Re-inserting into a shortened row rebuilds it.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.dropLast_le_getLast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.dropLast_le_getLast","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeRightInverse.lean#L71-L81","doc":"Everything before the last entry of a sorted row is `≤` it.\n\n`List.sorted_append` does not exist at this Mathlib pin; `List.Sorted` unfolds to `List.Pairwise`,\nso `List.pairwise_append` is the lemma that applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_of_forall_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rowInsert_of_forall_le","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCascadeRightInverse.lean#L60-L69","doc":"**Insertion above the whole row appends.** If every entry is `≤ x`, `rowInsert` finds nothing\nto bump and puts `x` at the end. ","signatureChunk":0}]}